        "dimensions": {
          "identity_construction": {
            "verdict": "pass",
            "notes": "I inspected the original identity and component boards, registered construction frames, and the current five shot contact sheets. Amber fur, cream muzzle and belly, and viewer-right coral scarf knot remain recognizable. Torso/hip overlap, shoulder occlusion, wrist registration and transparent head edge repairs are present in the final frontal rig. Fixed family registration and cast scale are preserved. Milo back design reference is explicitly rejected for scarf-knot asymmetry; frontal construction excludes that rear drawing. This decision covers the supplied frontal cutout construction and its declared variants. Other viewpoints require separately authored components. Open paws and a limited registered muzzle family are intentional pilot limits; segmentation alone did not establish this decision.",
